  "causal_assessment": [
    "Every ordinary acquired proxy task is immediately wrapped in ConnectionPeer. Recoverable operation failures reach explicit stop; completed secondary failures are retained in FixtureFailures.",
    "finish_one_shot adopts its raw handle synchronously before returning the future, so dropping an unpolled returned future retains abort ownership.",
    "Actual first-head readiness drives the retained first request. Sibling is explicitly polled to Pending under a held challenge; both request futures remain lexical and their completed results are combined.",
    "Challenge and queued supervisors retain every accepted handler in JoinSet; owner cancellation drops that set and aborts children. Explicit normal/error completion signals watch shutdown and drains results, with accumulated errors outside cancellable timeout futures.",
    "Observer poison fails before the response write. One-byte probe distinguishes clean pre-head EOF from nonempty truncation and feeds the byte into the same 32KiB parser.",
    "Deadline preserves the same five-second bound/context and exposes the actual Elapsed. Both remainder readers retain unrelated I/O failures. Half-close reader is owned before any subsequent fallible work and joined inside the worker."
  ],
  "rejected_candidates": [
    "No detached queued request handle: retained lexical futures are driven by select/join and dropped on early exit.",
    "No loss of prior handler failures when timed drain cancels: cleanup accumulator is outside both timeout futures; join_next is cancel safe in pinned Tokio.",
    "No reduced parser byte bound from first-byte probe: the probe is chained back into original read_head and counted.",
    "No observer false green on poison: actual recorded first exchange precedes poison; response and completed concrete error are independently inspected.",
    "No success guarantee is inferred from abort-on-Drop. Outer timeout/panic/cancellation may interrupt explicit observation, as author states."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Source approval only; no Cargo, compilation, formatting tool, native test, lint, MSRV or full gate execution by reviewer.",
    "Root must run all forward_proxy callers and seventeen frozen controls on Windows and Linux. Baseline logs are author/root-attributed; this reviewer did not independently read native logs.",
    "Queued cancellation has source ownership evidence, without a new independently executed native cancellation control.",
    "Finite quiet observations and deliberate cancellation of a pending partial head are not permanent absence or parser-success claims.",
    "Support partial reads receive only stated ranges. Historical base owner is diff comparison material, without whole-base semantic coverage credit.",
    "Expected TLS-negative boolean and byte-at-a-time chunked fixture parser are preserved; no expanded typed TLS diagnosis or general parser correctness claim."
  ]
